=== SURVEY ===
Web source VisuallyHidden.tsx is the canonical sr-only utility: it renders content invisible to
sighted users but exposed to assistive technology, with THREE render modes —
  • default  : the bare `sr-only` span;
  • liveRegion: pairs sr-only with the announced-region semantics. `liveProps` is computed as
      `liveRegion ? { role: priority==='assertive'?'alert':'status', 'aria-live': priority,
       'aria-atomic': 'true' } : undefined` (priority 'polite' default / 'assertive');
  • focusable : drops the hidden styling on keyboard focus (FOCUSABLE_BASE
      'focus:not-sr-only focus-visible:not-sr-only') — the "Skip to main content" pattern.
It is element-polymorphic via `as` (default 'span'; e.g. label / a / div) keeping identical
hidden semantics. The file imports only `cn`; it extracts NO `t()` call (anonymous surface).
Data source (P1/S8 per prompt): useAnnouncer (the live-region feed the component voices).
Shared components: none. Charts/maps: none. i18n keys from source: none (reproduce regions).
Existing native: no VisuallyHidden/VisuallyHiddenPriority/VisuallyHiddenAnnouncer symbols
(no collision). `AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(_).post()` already used in-repo (the
native voicing API is valid). Canonical predecessor studied: shared-surfaces/AnnouncerRegion
(0001) — the sibling a11y surface backed by the same useAnnouncer feed; repo convention is
per-surface self-contained types (cf. ActiveFilterChips defining its own announcer seam).

=== REASONING ===
- The web component is presentational and (for liveRegion) voices announcements; the prompt
  requires a production-polished native surface reproducing its DATA, composition, states, and
  (native-chrome) i18n, with every state visible (no blank box). Chosen: a native
  "visually-hidden inspector / demonstrator" — the three render modes shown VISIBLY (the hidden
  sample card; the Polite + Assertive live-region cards with their computed role/aria-live/
  aria-atomic chips, fed by the announcer; the real reveal-on-focus skip link; the `as`
  element-kind row) — while performing the REAL assistive-tech voicing (AccessibilityNotification)
  and the REAL focus reveal (@FocusState), so the underlying contract is reproduced, not just drawn.
- Architecture mirrors the canonical AnnouncerRegion leaf, per-surface self-contained types:
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): VisuallyHiddenPriority (role status/alert + aria-live), Element
    (the `as` polymorphism, default span), Mode (hidden / liveRegion(priority) / focusable),
    Semantics.resolve (VERBATIM port of the web `liveProps` + focusable base + sr-only base),
    VisuallyHiddenFocusable.webBaseClass (audit pin), Message + Padding (the useAnnouncer rotating
    `counter % 4` zero-width-space dedupe), VisuallyHiddenAccessibility summaries.
  • Model: VisuallyHiddenTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default; VisuallyHiddenPresenter
    seam (native voicing boundary) + OSLog default; VisuallyHiddenConnection axis; Input snapshot
    (latest polite/assertive derivation); Resolved + Projection (loading/empty/error/data);
    @Observable VisuallyHiddenModel (binds the source, posts each new message once via the presenter,
    one-shot stale auto-refresh); VisuallyHiddenStrings i18n facade.
  • Seams: VisuallyHiddenAnnouncer (native port of the useAnnouncer module — subscriber set +
    rotating dedupe counter, drops pre-subscription calls), Subscription, Source protocol, Live +
    InMemory sources, AccessibilityVisuallyHiddenPresenter (posts a real AccessibilityNotification
    carrying the iOS18/macOS15 speech-priority: assertive→.high interrupts, polite→.default queues).
  • View/Views/States + Previews + strings + Tests/ModelTests.
- States rendered: loading (skeleton mode cards), empty (full mode catalog + friendly TSEmptyState
  note, never blank — the live regions read as not-yet-written), error (retry — web QueryError peer),
  data (mode catalog + recent log), plus the orthogonal connection axis stale/offline (freshness
  chip + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition).
- Rejected: porting Tailwind/sr-only literally (native has no aria-live — used the platform
  AccessibilityNotification + @FocusState reveal); a truly invisible surface (the P4 leaf contract
  forbids blank boxes — rendered the modes visibly as an inspector); direct posting from the view
  (routed through the presenter seam so voicing is unit-testable); HTTP in the view (bound via the
  source seam); reusing AnnouncerRegion's symbols (repo convention is per-surface self-contained types).

